Brazil's agricultural industry accounts  for one third of its GDP the country is  the world's biggest exporter of meat and  farmers in the state of maturg on the  largest cattle herd in the country most  of them are staunch supporters of  President Jaye bolsonaro who is running  for a second term they say he protects  their interests  our right to produce and Thrive without  the risk of having our Farms invaded by  the landless and the indigenous people  he's allowed us have arms to defend our  private property bolsonaro chose a small  party to run his re-election bid when it  ran low on funds Farmers like kohaya  donated thousands to keep it going  small and medium-sized producers rarely  dig into their pockets to finance  politicians we don't trust them but  bolsonaro supports us and doesn't treat  us like environmental criminals many  like myself have kept a percentage of  our lands untouched as required by law  both molsonaro and leftist candidate  Luis Da Silva are looking to win support  of those who voted for other candidates  in the first round of the presidential  election  was the right of Center candidate who  came in third  she says she's also a strong advocate  for small farmers but now she supports  leftist candidate Louisiana  [Music]  during Lula's previous government the  agricultural industry boomed but he also  financed Family Farm production now  Brazil still feeds the world but 33  million Brazilians are going hungry  many plots that were once owned by big  landowners are now divided among small  farmers who produce food organically in  this patch of land there are 30  different kinds of vegetables and fruits  like for example we have here a papaya  tree over there a banana tree there's  coffee there's peanuts lettuce garlic  all of these are produced without the  use of pesticides  183 families make a living in these  seven hectares they distribute their  produce to poor families and local  indigenous tribes or reclaiming their  lands but these families don't have the  same economic or political clout as  Brazil's powerful Farm Lobby  which is why bolsonaro counts on them to  keep him in power Monica yanakaval  Jazeera matogorosu Brazil
 

